WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:14.530
Beyond the heavy rain is a rainbow
hageshii ame no mukou kakaru niji wo mita

3
00:00:22.790 --> 00:00:26.170
I'll know the easy answer's a lie
tayasui kotae wa uso dato shiru darou

4
00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Vow not to back down to the shouting
dekai koe nanka ni makenai to chikatte

5
00:00:31.920 --> 00:00:35.630
I need you alone to understand tomorrow
anata hitori ni wakatte hoshii ashita

6
00:00:36.970 --> 00:00:40.770
You gave me the time of my life
yume no youna jikan kureta anata

7
00:00:42.680 --> 00:00:51.280
What do I look like? An ANGEL or a DEVIL...
watashi wa dou mieteruno? sorega tenshi ka akuma ka

8
00:00:51.570 --> 00:00:56.240
Beyond the dawn, beyond the dawn
yoake no mukou yoake no mukou

9
00:00:56.240 --> 00:01:01.740
There's so much I want to tell you
hanashitai koto takusan aru nda

10
00:01:01.870 --> 00:01:06.540
Filled with love, with love
ai kometa ai kometa

11
00:01:06.670 --> 00:01:12.460
That can't be written down in a letter
tegami ni kakikirenai omoi da

12
00:01:12.510 --> 00:01:20.890
A small hand in search of eternity
eien wo sagashita chiisana tenohira

13
00:01:33.980 --> 00:01:39.280
<b>"To the Sea Where My Father is!
The Future Bonney Chooses"</b>

14
00:01:46.830 --> 00:01:51.540
<b>Three 
Years Ago, 
Mt. Corvo,
Goa Kingdom, 
East Blue</b>

15
00:01:54.710 --> 00:01:56.470
Gum-Gum...

16
00:02:03.640 --> 00:02:05.470
...Battle Axe!

17
00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.040
Did you see that?! Wasn't it awesome?!

18
00:02:25.490 --> 00:02:28.540
Hm? Why are you guys freaking out?

19
00:02:29.210 --> 00:02:32.590
With this power, I can knock anyone down!

20
00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:35.590
<b>Monkey D. Luffy (Age 16)</b>

21
00:02:36.710 --> 00:02:38.630
Even Ace can't beat me!

22
00:02:39.510 --> 00:02:40.550
Dragon...

23
00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.190
You seem extremely familiar
with this country.

24
00:02:53.190 --> 00:02:57.150
You even ventured to a small village
on its outskirts

25
00:02:57.150 --> 00:02:59.900
and were watching a particular boy.

26
00:03:07.910 --> 00:03:10.460
Keep talking, if you want to see me killed.

27
00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.040
What do you mean?

28
00:03:16.090 --> 00:03:19.510
A child is their parent's weak spot.

29
00:03:23.760 --> 00:03:24.890
I'm sorry.

30
00:03:25.470 --> 00:03:26.600
I'll forget what I saw.

31
00:03:32.690 --> 00:03:36.320
Gum-Gum Battle Axe!
This will be my killer attack!

32
00:03:38.030 --> 00:03:41.650
I'll use it when I face really tough enemies.

33
00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:44.370
When I become a pirate, I'll have a crew.

34
00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:47.370
Then one of my crewmates
could get beaten and captured!

35
00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.620
That's when I'll use it!
I'll make them pay!

36
00:03:51.040 --> 00:03:55.330
Whoever the enemy is,
I'll attack with Gum-Gum Battle Axe!

37
00:03:55.330 --> 00:03:56.290
See?!

38
00:03:58.250 --> 00:03:59.130
What?!

39
00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.260
Don't worry, I don't eat weaklings!

40
00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.180
Ring, ring, ring... Ring, ring, ring...

41
00:04:09.310 --> 00:04:10.100
Who is it?!

42
00:04:17.940 --> 00:04:21.690
What was that presence?
It gave me a chill.

43
00:04:24.320 --> 00:04:27.320
I guess a beast,
like the lord of this mountain,

44
00:04:28.370 --> 00:04:29.290
still lurks here!

45
00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.170
Pirates have attacked a merchant ship
and are on the run!

46
00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.510
Eliminate the pirate ship!

47
00:04:48.010 --> 00:04:49.760
I'm here to help.

48
00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:52.100
Are you the ones
who were raided by pirates?

49
00:04:52.220 --> 00:04:54.730
They suddenly appeared
and took all the cargo!

50
00:04:54.850 --> 00:04:56.400
How is your ship?

51
00:04:56.520 --> 00:04:59.230
Don't worry!
The fire will be out in no time!

52
00:04:59.360 --> 00:05:01.320
It hurts...

53
00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:04.150
Stay with me! Hang in there!

54
00:05:08.820 --> 00:05:11.160
I'll take him to a hospital
on a nearby island.

55
00:05:11.290 --> 00:05:12.450
Bartholomew Kuma!

56
00:05:12.490 --> 00:05:15.210
What are you doing?!
Eliminate the pirate ship already!

57
00:05:15.330 --> 00:05:18.330
I'm going on ahead. You guys catch up.

58
00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:19.880
Thank you!

59
00:05:20.000 --> 00:05:22.130
Without you, he would have died!

60
00:05:28.340 --> 00:05:30.220
B-Bartholomew Kuma?!

61
00:05:30.350 --> 00:05:30.930
What?!

62
00:05:31.060 --> 00:05:32.850
Surrender yourselves.

63
00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:34.180
Y-Yes, sir!

64
00:05:34.310 --> 00:05:37.980
Guys! Return all the treasure!
Or we're dead men!

65
00:05:41.570 --> 00:05:42.690
"Dear Bonney,

66
00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:53.080
The world is full of more beautiful sights
 than any book or picture could describe.

67
00:06:02.540 --> 00:06:05.170
It is brimming with exquisite scenery!

68
00:06:06.970 --> 00:06:11.100
I want to see your face light up
when you see it."

69
00:06:16.020 --> 00:06:18.770
<b>Sorbet Kingdom</b>

70
00:06:19.810 --> 00:06:21.520
Nothing yet?

71
00:06:22.900 --> 00:06:26.110
Nothing yet?

72
00:06:27.530 --> 00:06:30.200
Nothing yet?

73
00:06:30.320 --> 00:06:35.040
He's probably busy with his work, 
and News Coo may have misplaced it.

74
00:06:35.160 --> 00:06:37.830
But Dad said he'd write me a lot!

75
00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:41.540
You must wait patiently for letters.

76
00:06:42.630 --> 00:06:45.300
I'm sure one'll arrive soon, Bonney.

77
00:06:51.220 --> 00:06:52.050
Oh...

78
00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:58.850
The newspaper and a letter.

79
00:07:01.270 --> 00:07:03.190
- Deliver to the church's mailbox.
- Yes, ma'am!

80
00:07:07.530 --> 00:07:08.490
Is it a letter?!

81
00:07:08.610 --> 00:07:11.530
No, just the newspaper.

82
00:07:18.330 --> 00:07:20.250
Another letter arrived?!

83
00:07:20.370 --> 00:07:22.920
Yes... How many letters is that now?

84
00:07:23.040 --> 00:07:27.500
It's about ten letters a month...
So we've already received dozens.

85
00:07:31.470 --> 00:07:34.260
How does he have so much to write about?

86
00:07:35.180 --> 00:07:36.260
"Dear Bonney"

87
00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:38.470
"Dear Bonney."

88
00:07:42.270 --> 00:07:43.900
What a bunch of crap!

89
00:07:46.440 --> 00:07:47.770
"Lastly, Bonney,

90
00:07:48.730 --> 00:07:50.320
though I've said it countless times,

91
00:07:52.200 --> 00:07:53.820
I love you."

92
00:07:57.370 --> 00:07:59.410
It's your turn, Pert.

93
00:08:00.660 --> 00:08:01.870
What's the matter, Bonney?

94
00:08:02.000 --> 00:08:02.960
Gyogyo.

95
00:08:04.830 --> 00:08:05.710
Let's fight!

96
00:08:05.830 --> 00:08:07.500
Again, Bonney?

97
00:08:08.550 --> 00:08:09.840
What about Jenga?

98
00:08:10.800 --> 00:08:13.130
Fight! Fight! Fight!

99
00:08:20.720 --> 00:08:22.100
You little...

100
00:08:27.360 --> 00:08:29.730
Bonney! Turn back to your original form!

101
00:08:29.860 --> 00:08:30.730
What?

102
00:08:30.860 --> 00:08:33.700
It's time to take your medicine,
Bonney-chan.

103
00:08:34.910 --> 00:08:35.610
What?

104
00:08:35.990 --> 00:08:39.030
Oh, thank you
for taking care of her every day.

105
00:08:39.080 --> 00:08:40.580
Would you like some tea?

106
00:08:41.040 --> 00:08:43.540
Oh... No, thank you.

107
00:08:44.370 --> 00:08:45.790
That's strange.

108
00:08:45.830 --> 00:08:47.500
Was I seeing things?

109
00:08:47.540 --> 00:08:51.010
Bonney looked like a giantess...

110
00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:58.050
Here, Bonney-chan.

111
00:08:59.640 --> 00:09:01.850
It's so bitter! I hate it!

112
00:09:01.970 --> 00:09:04.770
Bear with it. It's good medicine.

113
00:09:04.890 --> 00:09:06.850
It's just a bad-tasting candy.

114
00:09:07.350 --> 00:09:12.070
Grandma Conney, why do Bonney's abilities
have to be kept a secret?

115
00:09:12.190 --> 00:09:14.190
Just to be safe.

116
00:09:14.240 --> 00:09:17.820
A wise wolf hides its fangs.

117
00:09:29.290 --> 00:09:36.720
<b>Marines' Science 
Group, Laboratory 8</b>

118
00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:33.510
That's unbelievable, Doctor!
Is it complete already?!

119
00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:37.880
Yeah. Now all I have to do is lift the lab
and my brain into the air with Island Clouds.

120
00:09:37.930 --> 00:09:40.800
Well, half of the stuff you see here
is holograms.

121
00:09:41.350 --> 00:09:44.390
I originally intended to do this
with Punk Hazard.

122
00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:45.980
Nice head-cut.

123
00:09:49.020 --> 00:09:50.940
I feel so light, I could fly.

124
00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.450
Kuma!

125
00:09:57.490 --> 00:10:00.370
I heard you're going to
lose your free will.

126
00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.700
A human without free will
or a clone with free will...

127
00:10:05.750 --> 00:10:07.460
Who has it worse?

128
00:10:09.460 --> 00:10:11.130
Stop it, Stussy.

129
00:10:11.170 --> 00:10:12.920
You're human.

130
00:10:13.250 --> 00:10:16.340
What does it mean to lose free will?

131
00:10:16.470 --> 00:10:19.470
No matter how much
you claim to follow orders now,

132
00:10:20.050 --> 00:10:24.560
could you, for example, kill a child
if you were told to?

133
00:10:25.640 --> 00:10:28.270
In this research,
the loss of free will means...

134
00:10:28.310 --> 00:10:32.560
...the loss of memories from living as a human
and all human emotions.

135
00:10:34.320 --> 00:10:35.730
All right.

136
00:10:35.780 --> 00:10:38.150
The examination is over. You're all set.

137
00:10:47.830 --> 00:10:50.250
How do you feel?
Are you starting to feel anxious?

138
00:10:51.290 --> 00:10:52.290
No.

139
00:10:53.960 --> 00:10:55.170
I'm more worried about...

140
00:10:55.300 --> 00:10:57.380
You're not being honest.

141
00:10:57.420 --> 00:11:02.140
You'll lose your memories and emotions.
It's impossible to come to terms with it.

142
00:11:02.590 --> 00:11:04.890
Especially, if you have
someone important to you.

143
00:11:06.930 --> 00:11:12.020
But I'll ensure you retain a minimum level of
free will until it's fully complete.

144
00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:18.190
You have roughly a year until then.

145
00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.290
A letter again?

146
00:11:27.410 --> 00:11:30.120
As long as I have time,
I want to keep telling Bonney...

147
00:11:30.580 --> 00:11:32.580
...that I love her.

148
00:11:32.960 --> 00:11:37.050
Over the next year, I'm going to write down
a lifetime's worth of feelings.

149
00:11:37.800 --> 00:11:38.800
That's so sweet!

150
00:11:38.920 --> 00:11:41.760
She'll turn nine soon!

151
00:11:42.130 --> 00:11:44.050
I'm sure she has grown a lot.

152
00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:45.890
It hasn't been that long!

153
00:11:48.270 --> 00:11:51.390
"I don't know
when this letter will reach you,

154
00:11:51.440 --> 00:11:54.560
but Bonney, happy ninth birthday.

155
00:11:54.600 --> 00:11:56.900
I'm at Vegapunk's lab now and..."

156
00:12:00.650 --> 00:12:02.070
Bonney!

157
00:12:02.110 --> 00:12:04.950
Happy Birthday!

158
00:12:07.200 --> 00:12:10.040
Grandma Conney's special giant pizza!

159
00:12:10.160 --> 00:12:11.910
Yay! Thanks!

160
00:12:17.750 --> 00:12:18.880
So good!

161
00:12:50.290 --> 00:12:51.120
There's nothing.

162
00:12:51.660 --> 00:12:53.410
No letter has come.

163
00:12:54.250 --> 00:12:56.920
I'm sure one'll arrive soon, Bonney.

164
00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.170
Don't you know I'm nine...

165
00:13:06.720 --> 00:13:08.090
Daddy?...

166
00:13:11.260 --> 00:13:14.600
You said you'd write me letters.

167
00:13:35.660 --> 00:13:38.630
<b>Baltigo, Revolutionary 
Army Headquarters</b>

168
00:13:38.630 --> 00:13:40.710
Kuma saved us again?

169
00:13:40.840 --> 00:13:45.090
Yes! He helped us out of
a dangerous situation!

170
00:13:48.430 --> 00:13:49.140
Kuma-san!

171
00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:54.810
But he again left without saying a word!

172
00:13:54.930 --> 00:13:58.060
If that's what he wants, don't chase him.

173
00:13:59.480 --> 00:14:01.110
He must have a reason for it.

174
00:14:01.690 --> 00:14:03.320
A reason he can't tell us.

175
00:14:07.900 --> 00:14:09.410
I'm cured!

176
00:14:09.450 --> 00:14:12.080
Look! All the stones are gone!

177
00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.750
I'm happy for you, Bonney.

178
00:14:18.750 --> 00:14:21.000
You did so well.

179
00:14:21.540 --> 00:14:23.380
I wanna go outside!

180
00:14:23.840 --> 00:14:24.670
No.

181
00:14:26.300 --> 00:14:27.510
Bonney-chan.

182
00:14:31.300 --> 00:14:36.470
We were told to take care of you
until your tenth birthday.

183
00:14:36.600 --> 00:14:37.640
That's a lie!

184
00:14:38.140 --> 00:14:39.100
You liar!

185
00:14:41.440 --> 00:14:44.190
Vegapunk said I'd be cured in a year!

186
00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:46.030
A year has already passed!

187
00:14:46.820 --> 00:14:48.150
No!

188
00:14:49.150 --> 00:14:51.780
I'm cured now! Leave me alone!

189
00:15:00.620 --> 00:15:02.420
That's too bad...

190
00:15:08.420 --> 00:15:09.880
That woman!

191
00:15:10.340 --> 00:15:12.140
How could she do this to her?

192
00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:14.220
Bonney.

193
00:15:15.680 --> 00:15:18.810
Alpha and her associates
are Government intelligence agents.

194
00:15:18.930 --> 00:15:19.810
What?!

195
00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:22.650
She's not a nurse?!

196
00:15:27.820 --> 00:15:29.190
Apparently,

197
00:15:30.070 --> 00:15:33.410
she was out in town getting drunk
and talking the other day.

198
00:15:36.120 --> 00:15:40.120
She said you were completely cured now.

199
00:15:40.250 --> 00:15:41.080
She said that?!

200
00:15:41.540 --> 00:15:44.670
I don't know what her hidden motive is,

201
00:15:44.710 --> 00:15:49.880
but it's strange to keep you, a healthy person,
locked inside for another six months.

202
00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:53.930
It's also strange
that Kuma hasn't sent a single letter.

203
00:15:54.550 --> 00:15:55.720
Don't you think so?

204
00:15:57.470 --> 00:15:58.140
Yeah...

205
00:16:03.100 --> 00:16:06.020
I've already talked
to Gyogyo and the others.

206
00:16:06.060 --> 00:16:08.480
Make for the port, Bonney.

207
00:16:08.530 --> 00:16:10.990
Go out to sea and meet your father.

208
00:16:11.530 --> 00:16:12.820
I can see him?!

209
00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:25.170
Don't worry.

210
00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:27.460
You'll be able to see him.

211
00:16:38.810 --> 00:16:39.470
Oh?

212
00:16:40.390 --> 00:16:42.270
I'm returning to the palace.

213
00:16:42.730 --> 00:16:44.690
Fine. Take care.

214
00:16:50.360 --> 00:16:52.990
Gyogyo's group,
they're not ordinary fishermen.

215
00:16:53.030 --> 00:16:55.910
They're legendary ruffian fishermen...

216
00:16:55.950 --> 00:16:59.240
...who strike fear into pirates and beasts alike!

217
00:16:59.620 --> 00:17:02.200
They'll surely help you see your father!

218
00:17:02.790 --> 00:17:04.330
I'm outside!

219
00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:07.290
Dirt...

220
00:17:09.540 --> 00:17:10.500
Wind...

221
00:17:13.760 --> 00:17:14.720
Grass...

222
00:17:17.430 --> 00:17:18.390
The sky...

223
00:17:31.270 --> 00:17:32.480
The sun!

224
00:17:44.120 --> 00:17:46.460
Bonney is actually walking outside...

225
00:17:47.210 --> 00:17:49.920
It's a miracle! There really is a God!

226
00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:02.390
Let's set sail!

227
00:18:10.230 --> 00:18:12.690
Bonney! This way!

228
00:18:12.820 --> 00:18:15.400
Gyogyo! Totts! Potato!

229
00:18:15.440 --> 00:18:18.780
Look! I'm outside!

230
00:18:19.360 --> 00:18:20.530
Where is Bonney?!

231
00:18:23.580 --> 00:18:25.290
Queen Dowager Conney!

232
00:18:26.160 --> 00:18:28.000
But you just went out...

233
00:18:29.080 --> 00:18:30.500
What's going on?!

234
00:18:33.500 --> 00:18:34.840
I'm Bonney!

235
00:18:34.960 --> 00:18:36.210
You liar!

236
00:18:36.340 --> 00:18:39.590
Look at that!
I made the ship look like pizza!

237
00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:42.140
I love it!

238
00:18:45.560 --> 00:18:47.310
How dare she fool me.

239
00:18:47.850 --> 00:18:49.020
This is unforgivable!

240
00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.900
All right! Let's go!

241
00:18:58.780 --> 00:19:01.200
Hold it right there!

242
00:19:01.990 --> 00:19:03.280
It's Alpha!

243
00:19:03.410 --> 00:19:05.030
Quick! Accelerate!

244
00:19:08.120 --> 00:19:12.580
If the subject of surveillance escapes, I'm 
permitted to use any means short of murder...

245
00:19:12.630 --> 00:19:15.340
...to subdue her!

246
00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:18.050
That'll make it so much easier!

247
00:19:18.920 --> 00:19:20.130
She came flying!

248
00:19:20.260 --> 00:19:23.010
She uses the Six Powers,
the Government's combat techniques!

249
00:19:23.470 --> 00:19:25.100
If I get caught here,

250
00:19:25.680 --> 00:19:26.640
I'll be...

251
00:19:28.770 --> 00:19:30.140
For those aiding her however,

252
00:19:31.310 --> 00:19:32.900
no holds are barred!

253
00:19:33.940 --> 00:19:34.980
No...

254
00:19:35.480 --> 00:19:36.730
I don't want that!

255
00:19:38.360 --> 00:19:39.740
Dad...

256
00:19:40.280 --> 00:19:41.820
What should I do?

257
00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:46.120
Dad, what does Nika look like?

258
00:19:46.240 --> 00:19:48.580
No one knows, but...

259
00:19:50.960 --> 00:19:51.870
Nika!

260
00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:12.060
Distorted Future!

261
00:20:16.020 --> 00:20:18.270
You can transform! I knew it was you!

262
00:20:18.400 --> 00:20:19.480
Bonney?!

263
00:20:20.440 --> 00:20:24.200
They say his body
had properties like rubber,

264
00:20:24.660 --> 00:20:27.870
and he fought however he fancied.

265
00:20:34.040 --> 00:20:36.000
You shitty brat!

266
00:20:37.630 --> 00:20:40.050
Nika-Like Future!

267
00:20:42.720 --> 00:20:43.630
What?!

268
00:20:51.270 --> 00:20:56.150
The escape of Bonney, the hostage, was 
reported to the World Government at once.

269
00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:57.810
And the fishing boat in search of her father...

270
00:21:02.400 --> 00:21:08.280
...would eventually evolve into an infamous
new-era pirate ship, much like Luffy's.

271
00:21:27.890 --> 00:21:33.140
I can't protect anyone again
mata daremo mamorenai no

272
00:21:33.140 --> 00:21:37.940
It's my fault that the voice is fading away
kiekakaru koe wa boku no sei

273
00:21:37.940 --> 00:21:40.230
I don't even have time to look down
utsumuku hima mo nai no

274
00:21:40.230 --> 00:21:42.820
Gravel marks on my palms
tenohira ni tsuku jari no ato

275
00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:46.200
Start moving again, my ship
mata ugokidase boku no fune yo

276
00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:51.700
Though I can't fly in the broad sky
hiroi sora wa tobenai kedo

277
00:21:51.700 --> 00:21:57.580
I can light up the deep sea
fukai umi wa teraseru kara

278
00:21:57.750 --> 00:21:58.540
We
bokura wa

279
00:21:58.670 --> 00:22:01.040
EVERYDAY, can't let this be the end
EVERYDAY owarenai

280
00:22:01.040 --> 00:22:03.670
EVERYDAY, can't be defeated
EVERYDAY makerenai

281
00:22:03.670 --> 00:22:07.470
We have something here to protect
mamoru mono ga koko niwa aru

282
00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:09.970
This may not be what I expected
yosou chigai kamo?

283
00:22:10.050 --> 00:22:12.680
But we can't stop now
tomarenai yo mou

284
00:22:12.760 --> 00:22:18.020
We go on, sharing loneliness
kodoku wo ima wakeai susumu

285
00:22:18.100 --> 00:22:20.730
Don't be afraid
ojikedukuna yo

286
00:22:20.810 --> 00:22:24.690
I'm not the same person I was that day
ano hi no boku to chigau kara

287
00:22:24.780 --> 00:22:28.200
No one can stand in my way
dare nimo jama dekinai yo

288
00:22:28.950 --> 00:22:29.780
Now, move aside
saa doite

289
00:22:29.820 --> 00:22:32.410
Conquer the world, believe in the future
sekai wo seishite mirai wo shinjite

290
00:22:32.490 --> 00:22:34.990
Count up the nights
ikutsu mono yoru kazoete

291
00:22:34.990 --> 00:22:37.660
What did you see? What did you learn?
nani wo mite nani wo shitte

292
00:22:37.710 --> 00:22:40.710
To realize what was important
taisetsu na koto ni kiduita no
